      "writtenOn": "2025-01-17T15:03:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like renaming it to `DstReadStrategy` and having the requirement be represented as a bool.\n\nI think that the CommandBuffer will likely have some implicit state that will have been set by the RenderPassTask that lets it know whether or not it\u0027s in a dst-read required mode (e.g. it has the dstCopy or dstTexture to sample), so if a pipeline comes in with a strategy that can\u0027t be handled with its current state, it can fail then.\n\nThese would be error cases in Graphite\u0027s internal logic so I think it\u0027s fine for things to be asserts that everything is correctly wired up so we fail fast. That means we don\u0027t necessarily need a kInvalid strategy.  I also think that if we are in a mode where we haven\u0027t fully determined the strategy yet, it\u0027s pretty intuitive to start with the default of kNoneRequired and then upgrade as something requires it.",
      "parentUuid": "feab07de_a88c4522",
